    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_12b91e5d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: the_name's_todd..._retodd; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a man with Down syndrome smiling broadly, with the text overlay \"the name's todd... retodd\". The joke relies on the phonetic similarity between \"Todd\" and \"retodd\" (a play on \"retard\"), which is a derogatory and offensive term historically used to demean people with intellectual or developmental disabilities. This type of humor is harmful because it perpetuates ableist stereotypes by mocking the individual's condition and reducing them to a punchline. The intent is to elicit laughter through a crude, insensitive pun that targets a vulnerable group, potentially causing emotional harm and reinforcing negative societal attitudes toward people with disabilities. The meme's overall intent is to spread humor at the expense of a marginalized community, which is harmful and offensive.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_29fc7c10"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
